name: ydotool (helper)
group: helper
what: The virtual keyboard Dictation and Arrow Pad type through. Installed automatically.
why: Under KDE Wayland ordinary programs can't send keystrokes to other apps; ydotool goes through the kernel's `/dev/uinput`.
changes: `ydotool`/`ydotoold` (Arch Linux ARM, signature-checked), user service `ydotoold`
access: **Writes to `/dev/uinput`** (a virtual keyboard any program you run could use while it's running)
survives-updates: Yes (everything is in your home folder)
undo: `./install.sh uninstall ydotool`
